  <keyword>ansaribradley</keyword>
  <short_description>Ansari-Bradley test for equal dispersion.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>h = ansaribradley(x, y)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = ansaribradley(x, y, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[h, p, stats] = ansaribradley(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>ansaribradley</b> performs a nonparametric two-sample test for equal dispersion. Vector inputs can have different lengths. Array inputs are tested along a selected dimension and must match outside that dimension.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include <b>Alpha</b>, <b>Dim</b>, <b>Tail</b>, and <b>Method</b>. The <b>stats</b> output contains <b>W</b> and <b>Wstar</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[x = [1 2 9 10];
y = [4 5 6 7];
[h, p, stats] = ansaribradley(x, y)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
